   "1. **使用语义化的变量和函数命名**：清晰的名称能直接表达代码意图，让阅读者无需深入逻辑即可理解其功能。\n2. **保持函数短小且单一职责**：简短的函数降低了认知负荷，使开发者能专注于当前逻辑而无需处理复杂的上下文。\n3. **遵循一致的代码格式与缩进**：统一的排版消除了视觉干扰，帮助大脑快速识别代码结构和控制流。\n4. **添加解释“为什么”而非“是什么”的注释**：注释应阐明设计决策背后的原因，因为代码本身通常已足够说明其具体行为。\n5. **消除嵌套过深的逻辑结构**：通过提前返回或提取函数来扁平化代码，能显著降低阅读时的心理复杂度。",
   "Hello! Welcome to the team. Understanding the difference between **TCP** and **UDP** is fundamental to networking, and the best way to grasp it is by looking at how we send physical mail.\n\nImagine you are a company sending important documents to a client. You have two different shipping services to choose from: **Certified Mail** (TCP) and **Standard Post** (UDP).\n\n### 1. TCP: The \"Certified Mail\" Service\n**TCP** stands for *Transmission Control Protocol*. Think of this as sending a package via **Certified Mail with a signature required**.\n\n*   **Connection First:** Before you even drop the letter in the box, you have to go to the post office, fill out a form, and establish a \"connection.\" The post office confirms they are ready to receive your specific package.\n*   **Reliability (The \"Handshake\"):** You don't just throw the letter away. You get a receipt. If the letter gets lost in the mail, the system knows because the recipient never signed for it. You will be notified, and you will **re-send** the letter until it is successfully delivered.\n*   **Order Matters:** If you are sending a 10-page contract,",
